@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-search-or-ask
The bottom pill on Home reads "Search or ask Pully" and is the one way to find a pull
request: typing filters the list at once, a pasted link or a number opens that pull
request, and a question can be asked from it. There is no search icon in the header and no
"Open pull request" field elsewhere (rules 35 and 55; D7). The pill has no Ask button: it
keeps its ✕, and while the trimmed text ends in "?" the ✕ crossfades into the send circle,
which asks it, and back when the "?" goes. Tavi decided this in the recording of 16 Oct
12:10, 05:03 to 05:47 (no "Ask" button "anywhere"; N8), replacing the Ask in the pill.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] home-search-dims-what-is-behind
While the search waits for its first letter with the keyboard up, the list behind dims to
half the sheet's scrim and a tap on it puts the keyboard away; the dim starts with the tap
and lifts more slowly than it came. Once something is typed the matches show at full
strength and take taps (rule 103; H12).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] home-nothing-behind-the-pill
Nothing white sits behind the bottom pill: the rows fade into the page under it and the
pill carries its own shadow, on Home and on a repository's page (rule 74; F3).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] home-sort-beside-search
The Inbox's sort is a round button as tall as the search pill, beside it at the bottom,
and its label names the order the Inbox is in. The chips over the list are the three
filters alone (Waiting on you, Authored, All). On Tours the sort button leaves and the
pill takes the row (rule 114; H19).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-one-row-anatomy
A pull request row is the same in the Inbox, Tours, a repository and search, after
Claude's own list: a tinted square tile with the state's mark on the left (open, draft,
merged and closed each in its own colour; a tour's ring in the tile on Tours), nearly as
tall as a one-line title and the meta line with a little air above and below, and centred
on the row when the title takes two, the title beside it on at most two lines ending in an
ellipsis when it runs longer (`android-whole-identifiers`; Q1; rule 201), and one meta line under the title that starts with the
number and carries the author, checks, coloured diffstat and age, in fixed columns that
do not move when a digit or a name's length changes (rules 13, 15 and 36). A draft is told
apart by its tile's colour and no title says "[draft]". A context-free count ("7
sections") never replaces them. Tavi decided this in the recording of 16 Oct 12:10, 01:23
to 03:05 (N4), replacing the number-first row. A row's title MUST NOT run to three lines,
and a repository row does not show its labels (Tavi's pick on 17 Oct): "these
things should never have three lines ... the icon gets squishy", with Claude's PR list as
the reference for the tile's size (recording of 17 Oct 14:45, 00:03 to 00:59; Q1). Tavi
said on 17 Oct at 17:14 that he meant the title on two lines ("I meant the title should
also be in two rows"), which replaced 0.48.0's one-line title.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] home-no-avatars-on-rows
A row carries the author's name in its own column and no avatar or initial. The reader's
photo lives in the Home header, and the author's on the pull request page (rule 33).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] home-names-are-horizontal
An author's name on a row takes one line and gives way only at its end; it never wraps or
stacks a letter to a line. A stacked pull request shows "2/10" with the layers mark on the
meta line right after its number, before the author (rule 111; H15, H16, H28). Tavi moved
it there from under the number in the recording of 16 Oct 12:10, 00:49 to 01:04 (N2).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] home-swipes-commit
On the Inbox a swipe right opens the review as a full gesture that commits on release,
with the displaced row blurred a little (no more than the canvas's 1.3px) and nothing to
tap after. A tap opens the pull request (rules 17 and 32; F6). No row archives on a swipe:
Archive is only in the hold actions. Tavi decided this in the recording of 16 Oct 09:50,
01:18 to 01:40 ("I don't think we need archive at all"; M4), replacing the left swipe to
archive.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] home-archive-only-your-own
A pull request the person did not open has no Archive in its hold actions (recording
15 Oct 13:54, 09:42 to 09:53; K20).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] home-left-swipe-goes-to-tours
No Inbox row takes a left swipe: the swipe moves the Inbox on to Tours, so the pages move
from anywhere on the list ("we can actually allow this swipe, but from anywhere":
recording 15 Oct 15:37, 01:28 to 01:50; L1; every row since M4).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-hold-opens-actions
Holding a pull request row opens a sheet of its actions (Open on GitHub, Copy link, Start
a tour, Open repository and, for the person's own, Archive), with the app's one hold
feel (H17; rule 120).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] home-tours-rows-swipe-like-inbox
Tours rows mirror the Inbox's: a swipe to the left opens the tour from the right edge, a
swipe to the right is left free so it moves Tours back to the Inbox, a tap opens and a hold
opens the row's actions (Open the tour, Stop or Remove). The same row anatomy; a finished
tour's ring is a filled tick and nothing says "Read" (rules 56 and 111; H27). Tavi decided
the direction in the recording of 16 Oct 09:50, 01:40 to 02:04 (M4): the right swipe used
to open the review and the left one to remove.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] home-group-heading-lines
A repository heading has one hairline under it and none above, so the first heading has
nothing between it and the chips (rule 75; F1).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] home-pinned-headings-stay-whole
Every repository heading, open or folded, sticks whole at the top of the list when it gets
there; the next heading slides up under it and takes its place, so no heading is pushed half
under the chips, and at rest none is left half under the pinned one. Tavi changed this from
pushing the pinned heading away ("collapsed project categories not becoming sticky with the
top bar": recording 15 Oct 15:37, 01:56 to 02:15; L2; H13; K19).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] home-heading-chevrons-line-up
A heading reads "Name (count) ⌄": the count in parentheses right after the name and the
chevron right after the count, all on the name's line, and a long name gives way at its
end so the count and chevron stay whole (recording 15 Oct 15:37, 02:16 to 02:37; L3). Tavi
decided this in the recording of 16 Oct 12:10, 00:08 to 00:47 and 14:57 ("we swap it
everywhere"; N1, N35), replacing the count and chevron at the right edge.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-heading-name-opens-repository
A tap on a repository heading folds its rows, and a tap on its name opens the repository:
from the Inbox on its pull requests, from Tours on its tours (rule 53; H26).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] home-inbox-and-tours-side-by-side
The Inbox and Tours, and a repository's pull requests and tours, sit side by side: they
move the whole width with nothing fading, both in view while they move, following a drag
anywhere nothing else takes it ("It should move like screens side by side", rule 107;
H20).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-pages-keep-their-place
Swiping from the Inbox to Tours and back leaves each where it was: scroll, folds and what
is open ("It brings me back to the top. It should keep me where I left off", rule 118;
J9).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-scope-chips-rearrange
Switching the scope chips rearranges the list in place with motion. Tavi loves it: it
MUST NOT regress to a plain swap (DESIGN.md Keep as is; walkthrough 14 Oct 12:08, 04:46).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-repository-page-shows-at-once
A repository's page shows its first screenful at once, from the phone's last copy or the
server's store, never skeletons for seconds (H14; rule 51).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-repositories-can-be-hidden
The person chooses which repositories show. A repository switched off is left out of the
Inbox, of Tours and of the chip counts (F19; audit 15 Oct).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-profile-sheet-is-short
The profile sheet has no Commands row, no Open GitHub profile row (a tap on the photo or
name opens the profile), no server address under the name, no Check out a branch and no
Refresh (H21 to H24; F15, F17). It is the reference for the right style and MUST NOT
regress (DESIGN.md Keep as is).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] home-profile-shows-github-year
Under the photo and name the profile sheet shows the person's last year on GitHub: the
contributions as a number over a grid of the last half year's days, commits, pull
requests, reviews and the day streak, and the year as monthly bars. The numbers are counts
only, come from the server's `github-stats`, and show at once from the last answer with no
loading screen (recording 16 Oct 09:50, 02:06 to 02:16; M5).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-jev-asked-only-when-sorted
The Inbox asks for Jev's kinds and risk (`classify: true`) only while it is sorted
Riskiest first or grouped by kind; with neither picked nothing is asked (DESIGN.md
checklist 53; architecture, Jev).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] home-rows-carry-no-jev-line
An Inbox row shows nothing from Jev unless the list is sorted Riskiest first or grouped by
kind, and then only one short risk word on the meta line right after the number, so the
row is no taller than without it. A stacked row, whose place there holds "2/10", shows the
risk only as its stack mark turning amber when the risk is high. There is no "Feature ·
Medium risk" line under the title ("do not run it by default", rows "way too tall":
recording 16 Oct 09:50, 00:08 to 00:37; M1; checked again for N3, recording 16 Oct 12:10,
01:06 to 01:15). The word moved from under the number with the row's redesign (N2, N4).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] home-pull-for-commands
Pulling the Inbox down past its top says "Pull for commands", then "Release for commands",
and letting go opens Commands with no refresh indicator. Tavi is "very in love with
that" (rules 52 and 117; F4).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] home-pill-clears-the-gesture-bar
The bottom search pill sits clear of the system gesture bar and rides on top of the
keyboard when it is up (rules 47 and 55).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] home-bottom-bars-stay-on-pull
Pulling a page down for Commands moves the page, not the bars pinned to the bottom of the
screen: Ask and Review, the Diff's bar and the Tour's Ask pill stay where they are ("these
buttons should be stuck at the bottom even if I'm starting to pull", recording 15 Oct
15:37, 05:18 to 05:33; L9).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] home-row-tap-is-not-a-swipe
A drag a row's swipe has taken is never also a tap: a short sideways drag springs the row
back and opens nothing, so a row never comes back pulled aside or animating (recording
15 Oct 15:37, 09:28 to 09:44; L16).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] profile-numbers-at-once
Profile's year on GitHub shows the last answer at once, kept on the phone between launches,
and refreshes underneath; Pully asks for it a moment after it starts (recording 16 Oct 13:06, 02:56 to 03:04;
O6, rule 178). The kept answer is the current server's; another server's MUST NOT stand in for it
(review of PR 57).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] profile-graphs-answer-a-finger
A tap or a horizontal drag on Profile's days or months reads that day or month out in the
big number's place, with a tick per step, and a second tap on it puts the total back (recording 16 Oct 13:06,
03:04 to 03:18; O7, rule 179).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] home-hold-menu-names-and-groups
A row's hold menu is headed by its number, with a card naming the item (state, title,
repository and author, diffstat) the sheets' gap under the ✕, then its actions in two headed
groups, Pully's own and GitHub's (recording 16 Oct 13:06, 08:31 to 08:58; O19, rule 186).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] home-posted-group
The diffs agents posted to the account are one group of their own at the top of the Inbox,
"Posted by agents", its heading in the magenta accent, foldable like the others. Its rows
are the Inbox's row with a magenta terminal tile, who posted it, the + and − and the age;
a tap opens the diff and a hold offers Open and Delete. The group shows while the pull
requests load and when they fail to, since it comes from the server. There MUST NOT be a chip, filter
or tag for them ("we are definitely not adding any more chips ... You just group them,
maybe somewhere specific, and you can maybe color the group": Tavi, 16 Oct 12:47).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-chip-is-remembered
The Inbox opens on the chip picked last (Waiting on you, Authored or All), kept with the
settings the account syncs; Show closed switches to All for the moment and does not change
it ("whichever tab I clicked on last, when I open the app again, it uses that one",
recording of 17 Oct 13:26, 00:03 to 00:17, P1; rule 190).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] home-stacks-are-one-row
Two or more layers of one stack in the same Inbox section MUST be one row, where the first
of them stood, with the bottom layer's title and number, the layers mark in its tile, the
meta line's stack mark with the number of layers beside it and no words ("Just use the icon
we were already using for stack and type a 3 next to it": Tavi, 17 Oct 17:51), their worst
checks, summed + and − and newest age; a tap, swipe or
hold MUST open the Stack sheet listing its layers, each opening its pull request ("group
them into one row, and make the stack the row, and when you tap it can show you which PRs
are in there": Tavi, 17 Oct 17:40; rule 202). A stack with one layer in the section keeps
that pull request's own row.
